### Round 2 (2026-08-24) — GM-ruled

Confirmed by the second `/session-summary-consistency` pass on the same scene set,
adjudicated in the Ch. 48 Quote Rulings artifact and approved explicitly by the GM.

| Wrong | Right |
|---|---|
| casting so much energy | **casting thaumaturgy** |

- `casting so much energy` is a **four-word phrase of ordinary English words**. It is
  listed anyway because the phrase as a unit is vanishingly unlikely to occur
  legitimately, and both transcripts produced it identically for *thaumaturgy*
  (cleaned VTT 1185, Zoom .txt 343). Same class as the existing multi-word row
  `Raponium captured alphabucks`. Do not shorten it.

**Two further rows from this round went to their proper homes rather than here:**
`Soba` was added to the **Soma** variants row and `Bourd` to the **Brewbarry** row, both
in `## PCs`. See the note below on why `Soba` did not stay a Round 2 row.
**`Bourd` was removed again on 2026-08-26 (ch50 pass) — see the landmine table below.**

**Rejected this round:** `unruthless → ruthless`. The string is a safe non-word and the
GM approved correcting it *in the ch48 quote*, but a glossary row would make the fix
automatic in every future transcript — erasing a GM verbal tic by default. That runs
against the `cover all sixes` / `mock my words` rulings of the same day. Correct it
case by case if it recurs; do not automate it.

