- `Shapal` is the Ch65 "Alyss" pattern: a **name-shaped token with no referent**,
  present in only one transcription. Zoom heard *"wait, Shapal says, you are the great
  Vukradin?"* (cleaned VTT 1985); the second transcription has no such word at all, and
  renders the same construction cleanly elsewhere as *"She pauses and goes…"* The row
  exists to stop a later synthesis pass promoting it into a person — the Bucherton
  failure mode. Note the comma is in the **Right** column, which the parser takes
  whole; a comma in the Wrong column would split the row.
- `Mark Gordon` -> **Marching** is a **reconstruction, not a corroborated garble**,
  and the right-hand side is deliberately `Marching`, not `Marching on`: the transcript
  already carries the *on* (*"Mark Gordon **on** stage"*), so the longer form yields
  *"Marching on on stage"*. Caught by diffing a regenerated cleaned VTT against the
  current one — a lint pass cannot see it.
  and is the lowest-confidence row in this file. Gary, l.5009: *"Mark Gordon on stage.
  Who's stopping us?"*; the second transcription produces no name either, but a
  different non-name (*"we are going on stage"*). Two passes, two readings, no referent
  in canon. **Revisit if an NPC named Gordon ever appears** — at that point this row
  becomes a landmine and should move to the table below.

**Added 2026-08-28 — backfilled hand repairs.** Seven repairs were living only in the
cleaned VTT with no row behind them, so regenerating from raw would have silently
reverted them. Each is expressed as the **longest** wrong-form that still matches the
one utterance, because every one of them has a short form that is an ordinary word or a
GM-forbidden landmine. Caught the same way `Mark Gordon` was — by diffing a regenerated
cleaned VTT against the current one.

- `Bourd is intimidated` -> **Brewbarry is intimidated** is the surviving third of the
  removed `Bourd` row. The landmine table below records why the bare form can never come
  back: 2 of its 3 hits on this tape were *The Board Laid Bare*, not the barbarian. Only
  l.693 was Brewbarry, and lengthening the wrong-form past the ambiguity is the fix. The
  canonical carries `is intimidated` so the row does not silently eat those two words.
- `follow Valve` -> **follow Valphine**. `Valve` alone is an ordinary English word and a
